<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  task3_part2_dock_fire.xml - Task 3, PART 2 of 2, in MANUAL on the sticks:
  from where task3_part1_approach.xml stops (on the GREEN bay's centreline,
  3 m out, bow in) to the end of the boat's part of the task.

    1. WHICH BAY   the docking report needs the bay's NUMBER, and this run
                   does not have part 1's dock book (a new goal starts empty).
                   Give it: bt_runner_node task3_bay = the N of part 1's
                   "committed to bay N". Not given (0), it numbers the bays
                   from what the camera sees here - enough with one bay (the
                   pool), NOT with three: from 3 m the outer faces are cut off
                   at the image edge and never become tracks (the sim shows it)
    2. DOCK        StrafeKeep drives in on the camera and the LiDAR: square to
                   the face, the lower-right window on the nozzle's line, the
                   LiDAR range down to the WATCH range. Held there square and
                   still for 2 s = docked: DockingReport(bay)
    3. THE FIRE    AwaitFireTarget waits, at the watch range, for one window to
                   go steady RED (re-sending the docking report until
                   RoboCommand confirms it) and names it. The hold moves IN to
                   that window's firing range and aim; line up, fire, until it
                   reads GREEN (5 shots at most); FirefightingReport(window)
    4. THE REQUEST back out to the watch range; Advanced and Disruptive only
                   (go.sh tier=1 or tier=2): read the colour code off the same
                   window, then ResourceDeliveryRequest to RoboCommand and to
                   the UAV

  The hold runs in the guard band, so it keeps the boat on the window through
  every step, the waits included: in MANUAL nothing else would.

  WHY A WATCH RANGE AND A FIRING RANGE. From the firing spot the camera cannot
  see the upper-left window: in the 2026-10-02 close-range frames, with the
  camera 1.0 m or less from the face, it shows in at most 65% of frames and is
  cut off by the hull edge in every one (whole in 0%); nearer still the dock's
  indicator drops out of view too, and the timing stage (which window is lit,
  the colour code) follows the bay by its indicator. So the boat watches from
  1.4 m - the camera ~1.0 m from the face, both windows in view, the stern still
  0.1 m inside the 2.0 m fingers (the LiDAR range is from the body origin,
  WallRange.msg; the hull is 1.0 m) - goes in only to shoot, and comes back out
  to read the code.

  THE HOLD ALWAYS TRACKS THE LOWER-RIGHT WINDOW (index 1), the one in view all
  the way in. The upper-left is shot by holding the lower-right 0.45 m RIGHT of
  the nozzle's line (aim_bias -0.45: StrafeKeep's lateral_bias_m, + = the shot
  further RIGHT): 0.45 m, the build guide's centres (0.22 m left and 0.23 m right of the face centre; the
  sim's WINDOW_SLOTS). The labelled practice-dock faces put it at 0.37-0.45 m,
  depending on how wide the face really is under its labelled box. MEASURE IT
  on the dock: tape, centre to centre, horizontally.

  THE NUMBERS
    watch range    1.4 m (above). Inside the fingers by 0.1 m only: check on a
                   real slip, and keep it at most finger length - 0.5 - margin.
    firing range   upper-left (index 0) 1.0 m, lower-right (index 1) 0.8 m:
                   squirt_cal 2026-09-28, nozzle at 30 deg. The 0.8 is that
                   day's estimate, never shot: calibrate it before trusting it.
    aim_bias       upper-left -0.45 m, lower-right 0 (StrafeKeep
                   lateral_bias_m: + = the shot further RIGHT). The measured
                   spacing replaces the 0.45.
    gains          the 2026-10-02 pool tune (at 1.6 m). Two of that tune are
                   bt_runner_node parameters, not ports: pass
                   strafe.window_median_s 0.1 and strafe.rate_window_s 0.5 to
                   tree.sh with -p (docs/T3_running.md)
    range_check_m  0 (the camera-vs-LiDAR range check OFF), as in the other
                   fire trees since 2026-09-28. On the real dock with fingers,
                   turn it on and set face_setback_m once measured.

  NOT TESTED ON THE BOAT. The sim runs it (tools/task3_sim; the run lines are
  in docs/T3_running.md); the water has not. It relies on:
    * with three bays, task3_bay must be given (step 1). For the competition a
      person typing the bay in is not autonomy: the two parts have to become
      one run (task3_part1_approach.xml's header).
    * the hold docks on the bay NEAREST THE BOW: part 1 must have left the boat
      in front of the GREEN one.
  At the pool with no lights, step 3 times out after 90 s and the tree fails
  (the sticks go back to the pilot). Shots alone: task3_fire_manual_1p6.xml.

  RUN IT (MANUAL on SC, the boat where part 1 left it)
    tree.sh true false task3_part2_dock_fire.xml -p task3_bay:=N -p strafe.window_median_s:=0.1 -p strafe.rate_window_s:=0.5
    (N from part 1's log; the pool's one bay: dock_bays:=1, and task3_bay:=1 or leave it out)
    go.sh 600 tier=2       (tier=0 Core stops after the fire report)
  true false = the sticks but a DRY pump; true true only once the dry run is
  clean. Taking it back, as for every fire tree: SC out of MANUAL ends it and the
  bridge releases the sticks; SD up trips the drop latch; SB is the e-stop.

  WHEN IT ENDS the runner releases the sticks: the boat is the pilot's again,
  in the slip. Undocking is not in either tree.
-->
<root BTCPP_format="4" main_tree_to_execute="Task3Part2DockFire">
  <BehaviorTree ID="Task3Part2DockFire">
    <Sequence name="part2">

      <!-- Dock at the watch range on the lower-right window's line. -->
      <Script code="watch_range := 1.4; fire_range := watch_range; aim_bias := 0.0"/>

      <ReactiveSequence name="guard_band">

        <ModeIs mode="MANUAL"/>
        <NotDropped/>
        <WallRangeAlive max_age_s="1.0"/>
        <AttitudeAlive max_age_s="0.5"/>
        <DockCameraAlive max_age_s="3.0"/>
        <UpdateDockBook/>

        <StrafeKeep fire_range_m="{fire_range}" window_index="1"
                    lateral_bias_m="{aim_bias}" nozzle_y_m="0.0"
                    cam_timeout_s="0.5" face_timeout_s="3.0"
                    range_check_m="0" face_setback_m="0.0"
                    deadband_range_m="0.05" deadband_lat_m="0.04" deadband_yaw_deg="3.0"
                    kp_fwd="90" kd_fwd="60" kp_lat="100" kd_lat="200" kp_yaw="5" kd_yaw="0.5"
                    ki_fwd="40" ki_lat="10" i_max_us="100"
                    min_us="30" max_us="120" slew_us_s="200"
                    min_range_m="0.6" square_first_deg="10"/>

        <Sequence name="mission">

          <SetTask token="TASK_COORDINATED_LOGISTICS"/>

          <!-- 1. WHICH BAY: given (task3_bay), or numbered from here: wait
               (up to 30 s) until one bay reads GREEN in the book, then commit.
               Inverter / KeepRunningUntilFailure / Inverter is "run until this
               condition holds". -->
          <Fallback name="which_bay">
            <BayChosen/>
            <Sequence name="number_them_from_here">
              <Timeout msec="30000">
                <Inverter>
                  <KeepRunningUntilFailure>
                    <Inverter>
                      <SafeBayKnown need_others_red="false"/>
                    </Inverter>
                  </KeepRunningUntilFailure>
                </Inverter>
              </Timeout>
              <CommitSafeBay/>
            </Sequence>
          </Fallback>

          <!-- 2. DOCK: at the watch range, square, on the line, still for 2 s. -->
          <AwaitStrafeSolution fire_range_m="{fire_range}" range_tol_m="0.06" lat_tol_m="0.05"
                               yaw_tol_deg="5.0" hold_s="2.0" gap_s="0.0" timeout_s="120.0"/>
          <ReportDocking/>

          <!-- 3. THE FIRE: which window (watched from here), then in to its
               firing range and aim. -->
          <AwaitFireTarget timeout_s="90.0" resend_s="10.0" window="{fire_window}"/>
          <Fallback name="aim_for_the_window">
            <Sequence name="upper_left">
              <ScriptCondition code="fire_window == 0"/>
              <!-- Slide onto the upper-left's line HERE, at the watch range,
                   where the lower-right is still whole in view and the hull
                   has room; only then go in. A 0.45 m slide at 1.0 m put the
                   hull on the dock in the sim. -->
              <Script code="aim_bias := -0.45"/>
              <AwaitStrafeSolution fire_range_m="{fire_range}" range_tol_m="0.06" lat_tol_m="0.05"
                                   yaw_tol_deg="5.0" hold_s="1.0" gap_s="0.0" timeout_s="60.0"/>
              <Script code="fire_range := 1.0"/>
            </Sequence>
            <Script name="lower_right" code="fire_range := 0.8; aim_bias := 0.0"/>
          </Fallback>

          <Sequence name="shots">
            <ForceSuccess>
              <RetryUntilSuccessful num_attempts="5">
                <Sequence name="one_shot">
                  <AwaitStrafeSolution fire_range_m="{fire_range}" range_tol_m="0.06" lat_tol_m="0.05"
                                       yaw_tol_deg="5.0" hold_s="1.0" gap_s="2.0" timeout_s="60.0"/>
                  <FireBurst burst_s="0.5" flight_s="0.8" ack_timeout_s="1.5"
                             window_index="{fire_window}"/>
                  <!-- FAILURE until the window reads GREEN: retry = line up
                       again, wait, fire again -->
                  <WindowOut/>
                </Sequence>
              </RetryUntilSuccessful>
            </ForceSuccess>
            <!-- no burst at all in five tries is a failure, not a quiet success -->
            <ShotsFired min="1"/>
          </Sequence>
          <!-- Reports the window shot at. After five shots without GREEN it
               still reports: the window is right even if the fire is not out. -->
          <ReportFirefighting window_id_base="1"/>

          <!-- 4. Back out to where the code can be read; the request,
               Advanced and Disruptive only. -->
          <Script name="back_out" code="fire_range := watch_range; aim_bias := 0.0"/>
          <Fallback name="request">
            <Inverter>
              <TierAtLeast tier="1"/>
            </Inverter>
            <Sequence name="read_and_report">
              <DecodeResourceRequest timeout_s="80.0" hold_s="5.0" min_frames="20"/>
              <ReportResourceRequest/>
            </Sequence>
          </Fallback>

        </Sequence>
      </ReactiveSequence>
    </Sequence>
  </BehaviorTree>
</root>
